 Ackermann function is a classic recursive function originally formulated by Wilhelm Ackermann. It is well-known for its computability but grows very quickly. The function is defined as follows:

\[ A(m, n) = \begin{cases} 
n + 1 & \text{if } m = 0 \\
A(m - 1, 1) & \text{if } m > 0 \text{ and } n = 0 \\
A(m - 1, A(m, n - 1)) & \text{if } m > 0 \text{ and } n > 0 
\end{cases} \]

Let's implement this in Python:

