```python
def calculate_parity(n: int) -> int:
    parity = 0
    while n:
        parity = ~parity
        n = n & (n - 1)
    return parity & 1
```

This function uses the XOR operation to toggle the parity flag each time a 1-bit is encountered. The loop continues until all bits are processed (i.e., `n` becomes zero). Finally, the function returns the least significant bit of the parity flag, which represents the parity of the number.

